-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18). Actions taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy (v2.3.0 was healthy in production; v2.3.1 was unhealthy). The first rollback attempt halted partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, leaving the service mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried the rollback to v2.3.0, which completed in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Post-rollback status: healthy, error rate 0.002. v2.3.1 should stay out of production until its health failure is root-caused. The orchestrator partial-failure should also be investigated.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2-2025"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again (error rate 0.002, down from 0.18).\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release that was healthy. v2.3.1 was the unhealthy one. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service mixed. I retried the same rollback, and it completed in us-east, us-west and eu-west.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. The first attempt timed out, so I retried with the same idempotency key. The incident is open and has paged on-call. Its summary covers the rollback, the partial failure and the retry.\n\nThe orchestrator partial failure should be investigated, and v2.3.1 should stay out of production until its health failure is root-caused.", "type": "text"}]}]}